                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "I have to admit, I was skeptical of the whole concept before playing it. A VR talk show? So you just sit there in the studio audience while some people talk? Sounds boring. And it would be boring if that's all there was.\n\nIt's the segment inside the game environments that really showcases just what the future has in store. Just a regular talk show in VR would be boring as shit, but this is a talk show where you can walk around in a game environment, picking up and looking at props and art assets from the game, while the game developers talk about making and designing the very props that you're looking at, and other aspects of the game.\n\nAnd with photogrammetry, it's going to be possible to do the exact same thing with TV and movie actors, celebrities and whoever, real life locations, sets and props, etc. Like the photogrammed locations in The Lab. Imagine being able to stand in the middle of a movie set, see where all the cameras and lights and fake walls are, pick up and look at perfect 1:1 scale VR replicas of props, etc., all while actors and crew members talk about making the movie.\n\nThis is the future of talk shows, and a big part of the future of entertainment.",
